    "created_at": "2022-05-02T14:20:45Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-05-02T14:20:45Z",
    "body": "- `<embed src=\"test\">` with early hints responses to the `test` request.\r\n- `<object data=\"test\">` with early hints responses to the `test` request.\r\n- `<iframe src=\"somepdf\">` with early hints responses + an `application/pdf` response to the `somepdf` request.\r\n- `<iframe src=\"test\">` with early hints responses to the `test` request where COEP headers disallow the outer page from embedding `test`\r\n- `<iframe src=\"test\">` with early hints responses to the `test` request where X-Frame-Options headers on the `test` disallow it from being framed\r\n\r\nIn all cases per the spec @noamr wrote:\r\n\r\n- The early hints requests added to the main request via `Link` headers must reach the server\r\n- The early hints request must not \"commit\", i.e. the substeps of https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#process-early-hint-headers step 17 must not run. I think this is most-observable by checking that timing information is not reported for those early hint requests.\r\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
