    "created_at": "2022-05-06T06:05:19Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-05-06T06:05:19Z",
    "body": "> Regarding `<embed>` and `<object>`, are these subresource requests? Currently the fetch spec doesn't expect early hints for sub resource fetch (Step 1 of https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#fetching). Are preload requests should reach to the server still?\r\n\r\nThey're not exactly subresources, rather \"special\" navigation requests. In the spec they currently don't handle early hints (see [navigate](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsing-the-web.html#navigate) 21.7, \"when resource is s response\", `uncommitted preload` is null). It would be good to cover that in tests.\r\n\r\n> \r\n> Currently Chrome intentionally ignores early hints for subframe navigation (`<iframe>`) to be conservative (avoid security/privacy implications which we aren't aware of).\r\n\r\nWe should have tests for this, either failing for chrome at the moment or to change the spec to allow early hints only for top-level navigations.\r\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
